From 183b892d99e4d6d3c219e9876cead40fee6498b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:40:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] tests: run every GCC-text diagnostic gate under LC_ALL=C

60bdc7d76 pinned LC_ALL=C on the subprocess calls check_warning_compat.py
had at the time; 3188d03cd then added three more (the kind fixtures, the
unknown-option probes and the object comparison) without the pin, and the
attribute and red-team gates never had it. All of them compare GCC's
English text byte for byte, and under a UTF-8 locale GCC quotes with
U+2018/U+2019. Measured on origin/main 0c51e3462 with LANG unset (Python's
PEP 538 coercion hands children LC_CTYPE=C.UTF-8): check_warning_compat.py
fails on the 'const' attribute row and check_attribute_diagnostics.py
reports 22 wording drifts; both pass with the pin. GitHub runners happen
not to hand GCC a UTF-8 locale, but scripts/ci_local.sh runs these gates
in the developer's environment.
