From e6789c1ebb7c364ff43ad5c2afc77a702413289d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:54:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] frontend: track pointer qualifiers; GCC 16.2 pointer
 conversion, conditional and comparison parity

CType erased every qualifier, so q2/q3 conversions (`char **` to
`const char **`) were silently accepted and no `-Wdiscarded-qualifiers`
existed. `PtrQuals` now records, per pointer level, the complete CVR bits
of the pointee when they are exactly known (CType equality still ignores
them; an unrecorded level never diagnoses):

* declarations, parameters (leading and parenthesised stars), struct
  fields (including the parser's folded simple declarators), typedefs
  (plain, pointer and array aliases), casts and function-definition
  returns record plain star chains, a definition's also when its stars
  point at arrays (`const int (*f(void))[2]`, whose `return` of a
  `const int[2][2]` into `int (*)[2]` was silent); `&x` and a named array's decay record
  the object's own qualifiers: a member's are the outer object's plus its
  own (`&cs.m`, `cps->m`, anonymous and union members), a pointer
  object's are its last star's (`&p` for `int *const p` is
  `int *const *`), an adjusted array parameter's are those inside its
  first `[...]` (C11 6.7.6.3p7), and a decayed array parameter keeps its
  element qualifiers (`const int a[2]` to `int *` warns);
* `int a[const 2]` is a const parameter: the parser kept no bracket
  qualifiers (`ParamDecl.adjusted_cvr` now carries them) and both
  parameter sites of the read-only checker hard-coded `false` for adjusted
  arrays, so `a = 0` was accepted where GCC reports "assignment of
  read-only parameter";
* `-Wdiscarded-qualifiers` / `-Wdiscarded-array-qualifiers` for
  initialization, assignment, return and arguments (transparent unions
  included), and `-Wincompatible-pointer-types` for q2/q3;
* signedness leniency only for the pointee itself (`int **` to
  `unsigned **` is an error, as in GCC);
* `?:`: pointer/integer `-Wint-conversion` and pointer/floating type
  mismatch; "comparison between pointer and integer";
* `-Wcompare-distinct-pointer-types` by C23 6.2.7 compatibility of the
  unqualified pointees, replacing 3188d03cd's emitter, which tested type
  identity: on 21 comparisons gcc-16 warns on 9; that emitter had 4
  false positives (an enum against its underlying type, `int (*)[3]` vs
  `int (*)[]`, a prototype vs an unprototyped function) and missed
  `int **` vs `const int **`; this one matches all 21. 3188d03cd's
  registry rows for it and `-Wint-to-pointer-cast` are kept, with the
  enum claim in the doc corrected;
* GCC's anchors: initializer start, the `:` of a conditional, the operand
  caret for arguments and `return`;
* parser: per-declarator/per-parameter qualifier leaks fixed; a nested
  group of plain stars in a parameter declarator (`int (*(*p))[3]`) no
  longer loses its stars (wrong `sizeof`, wrong loads);
* Display spells pointer-to-array and multi-dimensional arrays like GCC
  (`int (*)[3]`, `int[3][4]`, was `int[3] *`, `int[4][3]`), and
  "invalid operands" names operand types in GCC's spelling
  (`long unsigned int`, `__vector(4) int`, `int (* const*)[3]`); a vector
  compared with a pointer reports once instead of cascading;
* the parser's CVR_* star bits alias PtrQuals' bits;
* `typeof_unqual(type-name)` reports its exact (empty) own qualifiers,
  like `typeof_unqual(expr)`; `typeof(type-name)` stays unrecorded.

Gate: tests/regression/check_qualifier_conversions.py (115 GCC-verified
expectations, byte-exact against gcc-16.2 when present) in ci_local.sh
(fast) and CI. check_warning_compat.py gains the two new registry kinds (its contract
is one fixture per registry name; 17 kinds, 220 cases), and the
registry unit test lists them as measured default-on. Its corpus is
ill-formed by design, so it lives in
tests/regression/fixtures/qualifier_conversions/, outside the *.c glob
that run_regression.py compiles and links.
tests/regression/paren_param_declarator_depth.c (runtime).
